---
import Head from "../components/Head.astro";
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <Head title="Zoes – orchestrate coding agents across agents and machines (open source)" description="Zoes is a free, open-source coding agent workspace: one chat delegates work to Claude Code, Codex and eight more agents, hands sessions to another agent or machine with their context, and runs automations while you're away." path="/" rss themeColor="#09090a" fonts="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Geist+Mono:wght@400;500;600&display=swap">
    <link slot="icons" rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/assets/icon.png">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="demo/desktop.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="demo/phone.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="demo/screens/inbox.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="demo/screens/review.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="demo/screens/worktrees.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="demo/screens/board.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="demo/screens/automations.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="demo/screens/delegated.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="demo/screens/hosts.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="demo/screens/palette.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="demo/screens/handoff.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="demo/screens/fork.css">
    <script is:inline src="demo/icons.js" defer></script>
    <script is:inline src="demo/kit.js" defer></script>
    <script is:inline src="demo/desktop.js" defer></script>
    <script is:inline src="demo/autoplay.js" defer></script>
    <script is:inline src="demo/screens/sessions.js" defer></script>
    <script is:inline src="demo/screens/inbox.js" defer></script>
    <script is:inline src="demo/screens/review.js" defer></script>
    <script is:inline src="demo/screens/worktrees.js" defer></script>
    <script is:inline src="demo/screens/board.js" defer></script>
    <script is:inline src="demo/screens/automations.js" defer></script>
    <script is:inline src="demo/screens/delegated.js" defer></script>
    <script is:inline src="demo/screens/hosts.js" defer></script>
    <script is:inline src="demo/screens/palette.js" defer></script>
    <script is:inline src="demo/screens/handoff.js" defer></script>
    <script is:inline src="demo/screens/fork.js" defer></script>
    <script is:inline src="demo/phone.js" defer></script>
    <script is:inline src="site.js" defer></script>
  </Head>
</head>
<body>
  <a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>

  <header class="nav">
    <a class="brand" href="#top"><img src="assets/icon.png" alt="" width="24" height="24">Zoes</a>
    <button class="menu-button" type="button" aria-controls="primary-nav" aria-expanded="false">Menu</button>
    <nav id="primary-nav" aria-label="Primary">
      <a href="#tour-window">Product</a>
      <a href="#open-source">Open source</a>
      <a href="/docs/">Docs</a>
    </nav>
    <div class="nav-actions">
      <a class="gh" href="https://github.com/mingo023/anywhere" aria-label="Zoes on GitHub">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 0C3.58 0 0 3.58 0 8c0 3.54 2.29 6.53 5.47 7.59.4.07.55-.17.55-.38 0-.19-.01-.82-.01-1.49-2.01.37-2.53-.49-2.69-.94-.09-.23-.48-.94-.82-1.13-.28-.15-.68-.52-.01-.53.63-.01 1.08.58 1.23.82.72 1.21 1.87.87 2.33.66.07-.52.28-.87.51-1.07-1.78-.2-3.64-.89-3.64-3.95 0-.87.31-1.59.82-2.15-.08-.2-.36-1.02.08-2.12 0 0 .67-.21 2.2.82.64-.18 1.32-.27 2-.27.68 0 1.36.09 2 .27 1.53-1.04 2.2-.82 2.2-.82.44 1.1.16 1.92.08 2.12.51.56.82 1.27.82 2.15 0 3.07-1.87 3.75-3.65 3.95.29.25.54.73.54 1.48 0 1.07-.01 1.93-.01 2.2 0 .21.15.46.55.38A8.013 8.013 0 0016 8c0-4.42-3.58-8-8-8z"/></svg>
      </a>
      <a class="btn primary small" href="#download">Download</a>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main id="main">
    <section class="hero" id="top">
      <canvas class="signal" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <a class="badge-oss" href="#open-source"><span class="dot"></span>100% open source · MIT · no paid tier, ever</a>
        <h1>One chat. Every agent.<br><span class="grad">Every machine.</span></h1>
        <p class="lede">Run Claude Code, Codex and more in one native app. Delegate work and move sessions between agents and machines.</p>
        <div class="ctas">
          <a class="btn primary" href="https://github.com/mingo023/anywhere/releases/latest/download/Zoes.dmg">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M16.4 12.6c0-2.6 2.1-3.8 2.2-3.9-1.2-1.8-3.1-2-3.7-2-1.6-.2-3.1.9-3.9.9-.8 0-2.1-.9-3.4-.9-1.7 0-3.3 1-4.2 2.6-1.8 3.1-.5 7.7 1.3 10.2.9 1.2 1.9 2.6 3.2 2.6 1.3-.1 1.8-.8 3.3-.8 1.6 0 2 .8 3.4.8 1.4 0 2.3-1.3 3.1-2.5 1-1.4 1.4-2.8 1.4-2.9 0 0-2.7-1-2.7-4.1zM13.9 5c.7-.9 1.2-2 1-3.2-1 .1-2.3.7-3 1.6-.7.8-1.2 2-1.1 3.1 1.2.1 2.3-.6 3.1-1.5z"/></svg>
            Download for Mac
          </a>
          <a class="btn ghost" href="#tour-window">Watch it work</a>
        </div>
        <p class="fine">macOS 13+, universal. Also on <a href="#download">Linux</a>.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="agents" aria-label="Agents Zoes runs">
        <div class="agent-list"></div>
      </div>

      <div class="stage" id="tour-window">
        <div class="glow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="stage-grid">
          <div class="features" role="tablist" aria-label="Show a feature in the window" aria-orientation="vertical">
            <span class="group" role="presentation">Watch it work <small data-story-position aria-hidden="true">1 / 3</small></span>
            <button class="story" role="tab" data-go="delegated" data-dwell="14" aria-selected="true"><em>1</em><b>Delegate</b><span>Ask once. Three agents split the work, and their results come back to your chat.</span></button>
            <button class="story" role="tab" data-go="handoff" data-dwell="15"><em>2</em><b>Hand off</b><span>Move a session from this Mac to devbox with its branch and conversation, and keep going there.</span></button>
            <button class="story" role="tab" data-go="review"><em>3</em><b>Review</b><span>When an agent finishes, read its diff, commit and open the pull request beside the chat.</span></button>
            <span class="group" role="presentation">Explore more</span>
            <button role="tab" data-go="fork"><i data-icon="redo"></i><b>Switch agents</b><span>Move a chat to any other agent with its conversation as context.</span></button>
            <button role="tab" data-go="hosts"><i data-icon="server"></i><b>Machines</b><span>Add a Mac, Linux or Windows host over SSH.</span></button>
            <button role="tab" data-go="activity"><i data-icon="activity"></i><b>Activity</b><span>Every session across projects, by status.</span></button>
            <button role="tab" data-go="automations"><i data-icon="bolt"></i><b>Automations</b><span>Prompts on a schedule or a webhook, even with the app closed.</span></button>
            <button role="tab" data-go="inbox"><i data-icon="inbox"></i><b>Needs you</b><span>Every agent waiting on an answer, in one inbox.</span></button>
            <button role="tab" data-go="worktrees"><i data-icon="worktree"></i><b>Worktrees</b><span>A branch, a folder and an agent in one step.</span></button>
            <button role="tab" data-go="board"><i data-icon="blocks"></i><b>Board</b><span>Tickets across projects. Start one and it gets a worktree.</span></button>
          </div>
          <div class="desktop-frame" role="region" aria-label="Desktop preview">
            <figure class="window desktop" id="desktop-preview" role="tabpanel" aria-label="Delegate" data-screen="delegated" inert>
              <span class="lights" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
            </figure>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="caption" aria-live="polite"></p>
        <div class="hint">
          <span class="live"><span class="pulse"></span>Live preview</span>
          <button class="player" type="button" data-play aria-pressed="true">Autoplay</button>
          <button class="player" type="button" data-replay>Replay</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="tour" id="tour">
      <header class="intro">
        <h2>Status you can trust, <em>agents that keep running</em></h2>
        <p>Zoes hears status from the agents themselves, and a daemon keeps them alive when the window closes.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="tour-cards">
        <article class="card feat status-card">
          <div class="vis">
            <ul class="lifecycle" aria-label="Session statuses">
              <li class="s-working"><i class="spin"></i><b>Add dark mode to settings</b><span>Working</span></li>
              <li class="s-needs"><i></i><b>Fix flaky checkout test</b><span>Needs you</span></li>
              <li class="s-done"><i></i><b>Rate-limit the upload route</b><span>Done</span></li>
              <li class="s-failed"><i></i><b>Cache invoice queries</b><span>Failed</span></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="feat-body">
            <h3>Status you can trust</h3>
            <p>Claude Code and Codex report their own state from a terminal. Every agent reports it from a chat.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="card feat">
          <div class="vis survive" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="ghost"><span class="dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>Window closed</div>
            <div class="daemon"><code>pocketd</code><div><span><i></i>claude</span><span><i></i>codex</span><span><i></i>claude</span></div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="feat-body">
            <h3>Sessions that survive</h3>
            <p>A daemon, pocketd, owns every terminal. Close the window and your agents keep running.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="card feat">
          <div class="vis frame" aria-hidden="true">
            <b>3<small>ms</small></b>
            <span class="meter" style="--v: 0.36"><i></i></span>
            <span class="budget">of an 8.3 ms frame at 120 Hz</span>
          </div>
          <div class="feat-body">
            <h3>Native, not a browser</h3>
            <p>Rust on GPUI, drawn on the GPU, with a small Go daemon and no Chromium or Node. A Changes list with 1,137 files draws in about 3 ms.</p>
            <a class="more" href="/docs/architecture">How it's built →</a>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="handoff" id="handoff">
      <header class="intro">
        <span class="eyebrow">Handoff</span>
        <h2>Move the work, <em>keep the context</em></h2>
        <p>A session isn't stuck where it started. Send it to another machine or another agent, and it picks up where it left off.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="handoff-grid">
        <article class="card feat">
          <div class="vis" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="hand-flow"><span><i data-icon="laptop"></i>This Mac</span><i class="wire"><b></b></i><span><i data-icon="server"></i>devbox</span></div>
            <div class="moves"><span>2 commits</span><span>3 changed files</span><span>Conversation · 4 messages</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="feat-body">
            <h3>To another machine</h3>
            <p>Hand a session to a connected host. Zoes bundles the branch and uncommitted files, makes the worktree there, and moves the Claude Code or Codex conversation with it. Other agents start from a summary you can edit.</p>
            <button class="btn ghost small" type="button" data-watch="handoff">Watch it in the window</button>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="card feat">
          <div class="vis" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="hand-flow"><span><i data-icon="claude"></i>Claude Code</span><i class="wire"><b></b></i><span><i data-icon="openai"></i>Codex</span></div>
            <div class="moves"><code>anywhere_thread_transfer</code><span>fork</span><span>merge_back</span></div>
          </div>
          <div class="feat-body">
            <h3>To another agent</h3>
            <p>Ask a chat to carry on in any other agent: Codex, Cursor, OpenCode and the rest. It forks itself onto that agent with the conversation as context, and can send a summary of what it did back.</p>
            <button class="btn ghost small" type="button" data-watch="fork">Watch it in the window</button>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="cli-more"><a href="/blog/move-claude-code-session-to-remote-server">Move a session to a remote machine →</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="cli" id="cli">
      <header class="intro">
        <span class="eyebrow">The <code>zoes</code> command</span>
        <h2>Script your agents <em>from any shell</em></h2>
        <p>Start sessions, send prompts, wait for results and manage Board tickets. Agents can call it too, so one agent can hand work to another.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="term-window" aria-label="Terminal running the zoes command">
        <div class="term-bar"><span class="lights" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span>zsh — ~/code/orbit-web</span></div>
        <pre class="term-body"><code></code></pre>
      </div>
      <p class="cli-more"><a href="/docs/cli">Read the command reference →</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="iphone" id="iphone">
      <div class="iphone-copy">
        <span class="eyebrow">iPhone and iPad <b class="soon">Coming soon</b></span>
        <h2>Answer your agents <em>from the couch</em></h2>
        <p>A native SwiftUI app pairs with your Mac over Tailscale. Your code and your agents stay on the Mac. The phone reads the same sessions, the same chats and the same diffs.</p>
        <ul class="checks">
          <li>Approve a command or answer a question in one tap.</li>
          <li>Push notifications when an agent needs you or finishes.</li>
          <li>Live Activities that follow a running agent on the Lock Screen.</li>
          <li>Browse files, read diffs and check a pull request.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="phone-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="iPhone screens">
          <button role="tab" data-phone="sessions" aria-selected="true">Sessions</button>
          <button role="tab" data-phone="chat">Chat</button>
          <button role="tab" data-phone="diff">Diff</button>
          <button role="tab" data-phone="pair">Pairing</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="phone-stage">
        <figure class="phone" id="phone-preview" role="tabpanel" aria-label="Sessions"></figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="oss" id="open-source">
      <div class="oss-inner">
        <div class="oss-copy">
          <span class="eyebrow">Open source</span>
          <h2>Free, open and <em>yours to run</em></h2>
          <p class="oss-lede">Zoes's own code is MIT licensed: the desktop app, the daemon, the iPhone app and the push relay. There is no account to make, no seat to buy and no feature held back for a paid plan. There never will be.</p>
          <div class="ctas">
            <a class="btn primary" href="https://github.com/mingo023/anywhere">Star on GitHub</a>
            <a class="btn ghost" href="https://github.com/mingo023/anywhere/blob/main/LICENSE">Read the license</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <ul class="trust">
          <li><i data-icon="branch"></i><b>MIT</b><span>Read it, fork it, build it from source or use it at work.</span></li>
          <li><i data-icon="bot"></i><b>No account</b><span>It runs the agent CLIs you already signed in to, and never proxies a model or resells a token.</span></li>
          <li><i data-icon="laptop"></i><b>Runs on your machines</b><span>Your code, terminals and agents stay on your Mac or the hosts you add. The only hosted piece, the iPhone push relay, stores no device tokens.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="download" id="download">
      <header class="intro">
        <h2>Get Zoes <em>for your desktop</em></h2>
        <p>Free on every platform. Every build is on the <a href="https://github.com/mingo023/anywhere/releases">GitHub releases page</a>.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="download-grid">
        <article class="card">
          <svg class="os" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M16.4 12.6c0-2.6 2.1-3.8 2.2-3.9-1.2-1.8-3.1-2-3.7-2-1.6-.2-3.1.9-3.9.9-.8 0-2.1-.9-3.4-.9-1.7 0-3.3 1-4.2 2.6-1.8 3.1-.5 7.7 1.3 10.2.9 1.2 1.9 2.6 3.2 2.6 1.3-.1 1.8-.8 3.3-.8 1.6 0 2 .8 3.4.8 1.4 0 2.3-1.3 3.1-2.5 1-1.4 1.4-2.8 1.4-2.9 0 0-2.7-1-2.7-4.1zM13.9 5c.7-.9 1.2-2 1-3.2-1 .1-2.3.7-3 1.6-.7.8-1.2 2-1.1 3.1 1.2.1 2.3-.6 3.1-1.5z"/></svg>
          <h3>macOS</h3>
          <p>macOS 13+, universal. Signed, notarized and updated through Sparkle.</p>
          <a class="btn primary" href="https://github.com/mingo023/anywhere/releases/latest/download/Zoes.dmg">Download .dmg</a>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <i class="os" data-icon="terminal"></i>
          <h3>Linux</h3>
          <p>x86_64. Unsigned, no updater: download the new archive to update.</p>
          <a class="btn ghost" href="https://github.com/mingo023/anywhere/releases/latest/download/Zoes-linux-amd64.tar.gz">Download .tar.gz</a>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <svg class="os" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 5.5 10.5 4.4v7.1H3zM11.5 4.3 21 3v8.5h-9.5zM3 12.5h7.5v7.1L3 18.5zM11.5 12.5H21V21l-9.5-1.3z"/></svg>
          <h3>Windows</h3>
          <p>x64 builds come with the next release. Windows machines can already be <a href="/docs/hosts">hosts</a>.</p>
          <a class="btn ghost" href="https://github.com/mingo023/anywhere/releases">See releases</a>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="cli-more"><a href="/docs/install">Install guide →</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="faq" id="faq">
      <div class="faq-inner">
        <h2>Questions</h2>
        <div class="faq-list">
          <details open><summary>What is Zoes?</summary><p>A native desktop app for watching and driving many coding agents in one window. The window is Rust on GPUI, and a small Go daemon runs the agents. It runs on macOS 13 or later, with a build for Linux too. Windows machines can be remote hosts over SSH.</p></details>
          <details><summary>Which coding agents does it support?</summary><p>Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Grok Build, OpenCode, Pi, omp, fx, Hermes Agent and Antigravity. Zoes runs the CLIs you already installed and signed in to.</p></details>
          <details><summary>Can I run multiple Claude Code or Codex agents at once?</summary><p>Yes. Sessions are grouped by project and git worktree. Each one is Working, Needs you, Done, Failed or Idle, and Needs you, Failed and Done show in the sidebar, the inbox, the Dock badge and notifications. Activity shows every session across projects in columns by status.</p></details>
          <details><summary>Can one agent hand work to other agents?</summary><p>Yes. Zoes's orchestrator gives each chat tools over MCP to start delegated sessions, wait for them and read their results. Each delegated session gets its own worktree, can run on another machine, and wakes its parent when it settles.</p></details>
          <details><summary>Can I move a session to another machine or another agent?</summary><p>Yes. Hand a session to a connected host and Zoes moves its branch, uncommitted files and Claude Code or Codex conversation there. A chat can also fork itself onto another agent, such as Claude Code onto Codex, with its conversation as context.</p></details>
          <details><summary>Do sessions keep running if I close the window?</summary><p>Yes. The daemon, pocketd, owns the terminals, so agents keep running. Automations also run while the desktop app is closed.</p></details>
          <details><summary>Can I answer an agent from my phone?</summary><p>Coming soon. A native SwiftUI app for iPhone and iPad pairs with your Mac over Tailscale, with push notifications and Live Activities.</p></details>
          <details><summary>Is Zoes free and open source?</summary><p>Yes. It is MIT licensed, with no account, no cloud tier and no premium tier. The source is at <a href="https://github.com/mingo023/anywhere">github.com/mingo023/anywhere</a>.</p></details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="closing">
      <video class="butterfly" src="assets/butterfly.mp4" muted loop playsinline preload="none" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></video>
      <div class="closing-inner">
        <img src="assets/icon.png" alt="" width="72" height="72">
        <h2>Your agents, always <em>within reach</em></h2>
        <div class="ctas">
          <a class="btn primary" href="https://github.com/mingo023/anywhere/releases/latest/download/Zoes.dmg">Download for Mac</a>
          <a class="btn ghost" href="/docs/">Get started</a>
        </div>
        <p class="fine">Drag Zoes to Applications. Signed, notarized and updated through Sparkle.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="footer">
    <span class="brand"><img src="assets/icon.png" alt="" width="20" height="20">Zoes</span>
    <span class="mit">MIT licensed. Free forever.</span>
    <nav aria-label="Footer">
      <a href="/docs/">Docs</a>
